cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MOLRAPTOR: Molecular Fingerprint Rapid Generator"
version: "0.5.0"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
authors:
  - family-names: "Contreras-Torres"
    given-names: "Flavio F."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2375-131X"
    affiliation: "Tecnologico de Monterrey"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NanoBiostructuresRG/molraptor"
license: "LGPL-3.0-or-later"
abstract: >-
  MOLRAPTOR is an open-source cheminformatics package providing a Python API
  and CLI for SMILES-first molecular fingerprint encoding. It supports 10
  fingerprint algorithms with binary, count, and MinHash representations.
  Morgan is configurable, while the other nine algorithms use fixed effective
  profiles. Input order and duplicates are preserved, invalid records remain
  traceable, and effective profiles, runtime versions, input hashes, and
  profile hashes are recorded. MOLRAPTOR does not retrieve, curate, harmonize,
  or replace supplied SMILES.
keywords:
  - cheminformatics
  - molecular fingerprints
  - Morgan fingerprints
  - molecular representations
  - SMILES
  - RDKit
  - reproducible research
  - computational chemistry
